  "description": "<p>According to the spec, if an implementation chooses to reject requests concerning remote Group Listings, it must advertise the restriction with a rel=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#constrainedBy\" link in the Link response header.  </p>\n\n<p>To reproduce the problem:</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\n<span class=\"code-comment\">//Create a resource:\r\n</span>curl -v -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -X POST http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>\r\n</span><span class=\"code-comment\">//Create the following file: cross-domain.ttl \r\n</span>@prefix acl: &lt;http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#&gt; .\r\n</span>&lt;#restricted&gt; a acl:Authorization ;\r\n acl:agentGroup &lt;https:<span class=\"code-comment\">//example.com/acl&gt; ;\r\n</span> acl:mode acl:Read .\r\n\r\n <span class=\"code-comment\">//create the acl using the following \r\n</span>curl -v -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -X POST resourceUri/fcr:acl --data-binary <span class=\"code-quote\">\"@cross-domain.ttl\"</span> -H <span class=\"code-quote\">\"Content-Type: text/turtle\"</span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p> </p>",
